// Retouch merge — puts a repaired patch back into the image WITHOUT alpha blending.
//
// `repaired` is only defined inside the spot's bounding box (outside it Core Image supplies transparent black);
// `marker` is a plain opaque box covering it (alpha 1 inside, 0 outside) — deliberately NOT the geometry image: a no-input general CIKernel's output is not reliably clipped to its extent/crop in whole-region renders (measured). Selecting by that marker
// REPLACES the box's pixels (colour and alpha) with the repaired ones. `CIImage.composited(over:)` is wrong here:
// the repair kernels keep the destination's alpha, so for any source with alpha < 1 a source-over composite
// compounds the alphas (MEASURED: alpha 0.5 came out 0.75).
kernel vec4 retouchMerge(__sample base, __sample repaired, __sample marker) {
    return mix(base, repaired, step(0.5, marker.a));
}
// (`patch` is a reserved word in Core Image's kernel language — a kernel using it as a parameter name silently fails to
// compile and `CIColorKernel(source:)` returns nil.)
